   funEstim <- function(model){
       sem(model, data = df, group = "grpvar", estimator = "MLM")
   fits <- lapply(semModel, funEstim)
   residuals <- lapply(fits, function(x) resid(x, "obs"))

The resulting object residuals is a list of lavaan.matrices and there's one for each group in each model. So I can extract e.g. model 1 and group 2 residuals by residuals[[1]][2]. But how can I make each of them data.frames without any hardcoding? Naive attempt of data.frame(residuals) did not work.

