You will get the covariances between x1-x3 because they are predictors. You will not get residual covariances from predictors. However, by default, lavaan treats predictors like regression such that predictors are fixed variables. Thus, they do not estimate covariances between predictors in the model so distribution assumptions on predictors are not used. Lavaan reports covariances between predictors for convenience but not estimates the covariances in the model.

